class:: ShaderWindow
summary:: One renderer-owned native window controlled from SuperCollider
categories:: External>Graphics
related:: Guides/SCShader, Classes/ShaderServer

description::
Represents the one native window owned by an SCShader renderer. Create it before code::ShaderServer.boot:: to select the initial logical size, title, placement, decorations, monitor, VSync, and cursor state. The renderer runs independently of SuperCollider and owns the actual window; this class is a loopback OSC controller, not a code::Window:: subclass and cannot embed into Qt views.

One code::ShaderServer:: supports one code::ShaderWindow:: in this milestone. A renderer can run on the requested monitor and can be switched to borderless fullscreen, but independently rendered multiple windows and dynamically changing monitors are not implemented. code::close:: closes that native window and therefore stops its owning renderer process.

code::size:: and code::position:: are logical display units. After a metrics reply, code::logicalSize::, code::pixelSize::, and code::pixelRatio:: report the actual window geometry so HiDPI code can distinguish points from framebuffer pixels.

Input delivery is disabled by default. When code::inputEnabled:: is true, mouse positions are normalized to 0 through 1 across the current framebuffer; mouse moves are coalesced to at most one event per rendered frame, while button, key, focus, and resize events are delivered as they arrive. Key names are window-system logical keys, not raw hardware scan codes.

classmethods::

method:: new

argument:: width
Initial positive logical width. Default 1280.

argument:: height
Initial positive logical height. Default 720.

argument:: title
Initial non-empty title. Default code::"SCShader"::.

argument:: server
Owning code::ShaderServer::. Default code::ShaderServer.default::.

instancemethods::

method:: size

argument:: value
A code::Point:: of positive integer logical width and height. Sends a resize immediately when the renderer is running.

returns::
The requested logical width and height as a code::Point::.

method:: width

argument:: value
A positive integer logical width.

method:: height

argument:: value
A positive integer logical height.

method:: title

argument:: value
A non-empty title string.

method:: position

argument:: value
A code::Point:: of integer logical screen coordinates. The window system may constrain the final location; inspect code::position:: after a metrics reply.

method:: fullscreen

argument:: value
True requests borderless fullscreen on the current window monitor; false returns to windowed mode.

method:: borderless

argument:: value
True removes native decorations in windowed mode.

method:: monitor

argument:: value
A zero-based non-negative monitor index, used only when the renderer starts in fullscreen mode. Set before booting; changing a running renderer's monitor is not implemented.

method:: vsync

argument:: value
True selects the renderer's automatic VSync present mode; false requests automatic non-VSync presentation where the platform supports it.

method:: cursorVisible

argument:: value
Whether the native window displays its cursor.

method:: inputEnabled

argument:: value
Enables or disables renderer-to-language input events. Default false.

method:: front

discussion::
Makes the renderer window visible and requests window focus where the platform permits it.

method:: close

discussion::
Closes the renderer-owned native window. Because this milestone has one window per renderer, it also ends the renderer process; use code::ShaderServer.quit:: when process lifecycle is the intended operation.

method:: requestMetrics

discussion::
Requests a fresh metrics reply. The class also receives one after readiness and after a supported runtime property change.

method:: logicalSize

returns::
The latest actual logical client-area size as a code::Point::.

method:: pixelSize

returns::
The latest actual framebuffer size as a code::Point::.

method:: pixelRatio

returns::
The latest framebuffer-pixels-per-logical-unit scale factor.

method:: mouseMoveAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, normalizedPosition| ... }::. Mouse motion is coalesced to at most once per rendered frame.

method:: mouseDownAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, normalizedPosition, button| ... }::. Button values are 0 left, 1 right, 2 middle, 3 back, 4 forward, or the platform's other button value.

method:: mouseUpAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called with the same arguments as code::mouseDownAction::.

method:: keyDownAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, key, repeat| ... }::. code::key:: is a logical key-name string and code::repeat:: is a Boolean.

method:: keyUpAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, key, repeat| ... }::.

method:: resizeAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, logicalSize, pixelSize, pixelRatio| ... }::. This requires code::inputEnabled::.

method:: focusAction

argument:: function
An optional Function called as code::{ |window, focused| ... }::. This requires code::inputEnabled::.

examples::

This example uses the packaged extension. Run one demo at a time and wait for setup to finish. It creates its own resources; no earlier example is required. See link::Guides/SCShader:: for the full walkthrough.

code::
(
v = ShaderServer.new(\guideWindow);
w = ShaderWindow.new(960, 540, "SCShader", v);
w.inputEnabled_(true);
w.mouseDownAction_({ |window, point, button| [point, button].postln });
v.waitForBoot { |server|
    server.status { |receiver, status| status.postln };
};
)
::

Cleanup before starting another example; wait for any renderer window to close:

code::
(
w.free; v.free;
)
::

